port x11/babl
type port
reason "DragonFly: keep babl off its AVX-512 (x86-64-v4) paths"

# 0.1.128 (2026Q4 on) adds x86-64-v4 code and turns it on from CPUID
# alone. DragonFly does not enable AVX-512 register state, so on an
# AVX-512 CPU the first such instruction raises SIGILL (gegl, run by
# graphics/gimp-app's build, died that way). dragonfly/@2026Q4 and @main
# never set the AVX512* caps on DragonFly; babl stays on x86-64-v3.
